      "id": "table-2",
      "line": 114,
      "heading_context": "## Old World -> New World Bridge",
      "headers": [
        "You know (C++/.NET/general CS)",
        "Rust makes it a checked type-system fact"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "RAII / destructors (C++), `IDisposable`/`using` (.NET)",
          "`Drop` runs deterministically at scope end — no `using` needed, no GC finalizer nondeterminism"
        ],
        [
          "`const T&` vs `T&` (C++ const correctness)",
          "`&T` vs `&mut T`, enforced globally, not per-call convention"
        ],
        [
          "`std::move`, move constructors",
          "Moves are the *default*; the moved-from binding is statically dead"
        ],
        [
          "`shared_ptr` / `unique_ptr`",
          "`Arc`/`Rc` and `Box` — but thread-safety is a type property (`Send`/`Sync`)"
        ],
        [
          "Nullable references, `Nullable<T>`",
          "`Option<T>` — no null, exhaustiveness forces handling"
        ],
        [
          "Exceptions",
          "`Result<T, E>` + `?` — errors are values in the signature"
        ],
        [
          "Interfaces / abstract classes",
          "Traits — but with associated types, blanket impls, coherence"
        ],
        [
          "Generics (erased in Java/C#)",
          "Generics monomorphize like C++ templates (no vtable unless `dyn`)"
        ]
      ]
    },
